---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy - Achint Satsangi" description="What this site counts, who processes it, and how to switch it off.">
  <section class="page hero-inner">
    <h1 class="display-lg max-w-5xl" data-testid="privacy-hero">Privacy.</h1>
    <div class="mt-10 max-w-3xl space-y-6 body-lg text-muted dark:text-muted-dark">
      <p><span class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark font-medium">Who.</span> This site is run by me, Achint Satsangi, in Oslo, Norway. I'm responsible for the data it collects. Contact: <a href="mailto:achint.satsangi@gmail.com" class="text-accent dark:text-accent-dark">achint.satsangi@gmail.com</a>.</p>
      <p><span class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark font-medium">What and why.</span> If you say yes, Google Analytics counts which pages you visit and what you click, plus rough location, device and browser. I use it only to see what people read, so I know what's worth writing more of. Nothing loads from Google until you say yes. Not used for ads, never sold.</p>
      <p><span class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark font-medium">Legal basis.</span> Your consent (GDPR Art. 6(1)(a) and the Norwegian Electronic Communications Act). Saying no changes nothing about what you can read here.</p>
      <p><span class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark font-medium">Who processes it.</span> Google processes the data on my behalf as a data processor. Data may be transferred to the US under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework. Analytics data is kept for 14 months.</p>
      <p><span class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark font-medium">Cookies and storage.</span> With your yes, Google Analytics sets <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code> cookies that last up to 13 months. Your choice itself is saved in your browser's local storage as <code>analytics-consent</code>, so the question doesn't come back on every page. That needs no consent and never leaves your browser.</p>
      <p><span class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark font-medium">Your rights.</span> You can withdraw consent any time with the "Analytics" button at the bottom of every page; it also deletes the analytics cookies. Withdrawing doesn't affect what was counted before. You can ask me for access to or deletion of data about you, and you can complain to the Norwegian Data Protection Authority, <a href="https://www.datatilsynet.no/en/" class="text-accent dark:text-accent-dark">Datatilsynet</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
